<title>CONGO: Congo liberalises telecommunications.</title>
<headline>Congo liberalises telecommunications.</headline>
<dateline>BRAZZAVILLE 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The national assembly approved regulations that liberalise telecommunications and pave the way for eventual privatisation, state Radio Congo reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Posts and telecommunications will be split and the state will retain a monopoly over basic telephone and telex services for seven years.</p>
<p>New products such as mobile phones and satellite services will be liberalised, the radio said.</p>
</text>
